{
  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most important uncertainty is whether the full multimodal pipeline (best RNA encoder + best image encoder + expressive aggregation + multiprofile data) can achieve high validation accuracy, establishing a performance ceiling. config_001 (scgpt + imagenet_vit_l + transformer aggregation + concat fusion, multiprofile) is the strongest 'full-featured' multimodal configuration available. Testing it first gives the highest information gain: if it performs well, subsequent experiments can ablate individual components (e.g., swap ViT-L→ResNet50, transformer→avgpool, multiprofile→singleprofile) to identify which design choices drive accuracy; if it underperforms, I immediately know the ceiling is lower and should explore simpler or unimodal alternatives. This is the most expensive configuration (scgpt is a large generative pretrained encoder, ViT-L is a large vision transformer, transformer aggregation adds parameters, and multiprofile increases sequence length), so I expect it to be roughly 2–3× the GPU-hours of a singleprofile/ResNet50/avgpool baseline. However, as experiment 1 of 10, establishing the upper bound is the single most valuable piece of information for directing the remaining 9 experiments efficiently."
}

